WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:19.630
Soon Zann was in the girls' room, showing them the message moth and telling them about the password.

2
00:00:19.631 --> 00:00:22.611
Darb was with him, yawning and confused.

3
00:00:22.612 --> 00:00:28.759
"I don't understand," Gliss said sleepily. "Who sent you this message?"

4
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:34.813
"I bet it was Yog." Perda rubbed her eyes. "I think he wants to help us."

5
00:00:34.814 --> 00:00:39.874
"But if it was Yog, why wouldn't he have just let us out earlier?" Darb wondered.

6
00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:44.302
"Who cares?" Zann said. "Let's see if the password works!"

7
00:00:44.303 --> 00:00:48.913
"Are you crazy?" Gliss said, sounding more awake now.

8
00:00:48.914 --> 00:00:52.588
"If we use magic, Morb will be able to track us!"

9
00:00:52.589 --> 00:00:56.167
"Only if he's still paying attention," Perda argued.

10
00:00:56.168 --> 00:00:58.853
"Don't you remember what Yog told us?

11
00:00:58.854 --> 00:01:02.951
He said the trolls aren't zapping their Red prisoners away anymore.

12
00:01:02.952 --> 00:01:08.170
Maybe that means Morb used up all his power when he captured the king and queen."

13
00:01:08.171 --> 00:01:11.178
"Or maybe he didn't." Darb looked thoughtful.

14
00:01:11.179 --> 00:01:15.437
"We really have no idea why the trolls are keeping people at the zoo."

15
00:01:15.438 --> 00:01:19.028
Zann released the message moth and turned back to his friends.

16
00:01:19.029 --> 00:01:25.731
"I know one thing—we're not going to find Boz's Magic Master friends if we're stuck in the palace.

17
00:01:25.732 --> 00:01:32.103
And we need their help. I'm willing to take a risk and use magic to get out of here."

18
00:01:32.104 --> 00:01:35.446
"Me too," Perda said. "But we should hurry.

19
00:01:35.447 --> 00:01:38.286
Yog will be here soon to make our breakfast."

20
00:01:38.287 --> 00:01:46.275
Zann nodded. "Yeah, and if he's not the one who sent us the password, we don't want to be here when he arrives."

21
00:01:46.276 --> 00:01:49.660
Gliss hesitated. "I want to find my parents.

22
00:01:49.661 --> 00:01:55.811
But I think it might be better to just stay here and let the grown-ups figure out what to do." She shivered.

23
00:01:55.812 --> 00:01:59.471
"Plus I'm still worried that Morb might catch us."

24
00:01:59.472 --> 00:02:01.852
"Maybe she's right," Darb said.

25
00:02:01.853 --> 00:02:05.478
"He hasn't caught us so far," Zann pointed out.

26
00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:10.062
"Anyway, isn't it worth a little risk to find Boz's friends?

27
00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:18.029
Boz was always telling me stories about them, especially Teplo, who's supposed to be some kind of magical genius.

28
00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:23.055
A guy like that is much more likely to have a good plan than Slib."

29
00:02:23.056 --> 00:02:26.958
"Right," Perda agreed. "I say we go for it!"

30
00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:30.160
"Well . . ." Gliss still looked uncertain.

31
00:02:30.161 --> 00:02:35.710
"If you think we can get out of the palace without getting caught, I guess I'll go."

32
00:02:35.711 --> 00:02:41.490
"We'll be fine," Zann assured her. "But to play it safe, let's split up.

33
00:02:41.491 --> 00:02:46.186
Morb probably can't track all of us if we zap to different places.

34
00:02:46.187 --> 00:02:48.481
Then we can meet up on foot."

35
00:02:48.482 --> 00:02:53.656
"Split up?" Gliss said anxiously. "I don't want to go alone!"

36
00:02:53.657 --> 00:02:58.840
"You can take Darb with you," Zann said. "It's better if I zap alone anyway.

37
00:02:58.841 --> 00:03:03.659
Because if Morb is going to come after anyone, it will probably be me."

38
00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:07.177
"Smart plan," Perda agreed. "What do you say, Gliss?"

39
00:03:07.178 --> 00:03:12.343
Gliss bit her lip. "Okay," she said in a small voice. "I'll do it."

40
00:03:12.344 --> 00:03:16.757
"Good. Perda, Gliss, here's where you should focus on landing . . ."

41
00:03:16.758 --> 00:03:19.903
Zann described two spots in his old neighborhood.

42
00:03:19.904 --> 00:03:23.496
They all got dressed and then gathered again in the main room.

43
00:03:23.497 --> 00:03:28.534
Darb held on to Gliss' elbow while she, Zann, and Perda formed a circle.

44
00:03:28.535 --> 00:03:36.127
Zann touched one palm to Perda's right hand and the other to Gliss' left. Soon sparks were flying.

45
00:03:36.128 --> 00:03:41.195
"Focus on the places I told you about," Zann reminded them. "Zipflower!"

46
00:03:41.196 --> 00:03:43.057
Zap!

47
00:03:43.058 --> 00:03:44.576
Splash!

48
00:03:44.577 --> 00:03:51.355
"Oh man!" Zann moaned, looking down. He'd planned on landing at the corner near his old house.

49
00:03:51.356 --> 00:03:55.824
Instead he landed a short distance away in a fountain.

50
00:03:55.825 --> 00:03:59.732
But he forgot about his wet feet when he heard a loud grunt.

51
00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:03.163
Two huge trolls were charging right toward him!

52
00:04:03.164 --> 00:04:06.235
Leaping out of the fountain, Zann took off running.

53
00:04:06.236 --> 00:04:10.754
The trolls thundered after him, grunting to each other in their own language.

54
00:04:10.755 --> 00:04:13.669
Zann dashed out of the park and down a side street.

55
00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:18.009
Behind him he could hear the trolls getting closer with every step.

56
00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:22.784
Even though trolls were big and heavy, they could run fast when they wanted to.

57
00:04:22.785 --> 00:04:25.681
But they didn't know this neighborhood the way Zann did.

58
00:04:25.682 --> 00:04:32.350
He dashed down an even smaller street and vaulted over a garden wall before the trolls rounded the corner.

59
00:04:32.351 --> 00:04:39.623
He could hear them grunting with anger and confusion as he tiptoed across the garden and out the gate on the far side.

60
00:04:39.624 --> 00:04:44.287
As soon as Zann was sure that he'd lost the trolls, he jogged to the meeting spot.

61
00:04:44.288 --> 00:04:48.738
It was a quiet alley where nobody was likely to bother their little group.

62
00:04:48.739 --> 00:04:53.074
When he turned the corner, he saw Perda standing there, looking anxious.

63
00:04:53.075 --> 00:05:00.998
"Zann! You made it!" she cried, her face relaxing into a smile. "I was just starting to worry."

64
00:05:00.999 --> 00:05:05.542
Zann nodded. "Did you have any trouble with trolls when you landed?"

65
00:05:05.543 --> 00:05:08.506
"No," Perda said. "Did you?"

66
00:05:08.507 --> 00:05:13.546
"Yeah. I thought maybe they'd tracked our magic after all." Zann shrugged.

67
00:05:13.547 --> 00:05:17.051
"But Yog said there are trolls all over the city.

68
00:05:17.052 --> 00:05:20.508
It was probably just bad luck that they spotted me."

69
00:05:20.509 --> 00:05:27.656
"Probably," Perda agreed. "Now that we're out of the palace, we should try to find new disguises for you and Gliss."

70
00:05:27.657 --> 00:05:32.964
"You're right. And we should figure out how to get Zing back," Zann said.

71
00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:36.903
Perda nodded and then pointed. "Look! Here comes Darb."

72
00:05:36.904 --> 00:05:42.106
"Good." Zann glanced at Darb, who had just rounded the corner. "We did it!"

73
00:05:42.107 --> 00:05:47.165
Their excitement quickly disappeared though when they realized that Darb was alone.

74
00:05:47.166 --> 00:05:50.586
Zann's heart skipped a beat. Where was Gliss?

75
00:05:50.587 --> 00:05:55.417
When Darb got closer, Zann could see that his friend was completely terrified.

76
00:05:55.418 --> 00:06:04.077
"They got her!" Darb cried out as he reached them. "The trolls got Gliss!"
